One thing that slightly worries me here, with respect to any future code changes, is the need to remember to *manually* add these streams in order for things to work correctly.

To reduce the risk of future bugs, can we at least ensure that `this.appearance` will always be reset here? Something like the following may not be perfect, but should at least help prevent trivial bugs during development:
```suggestion
  reset() {
    if (
      (typeof PDFJSDev === "undefined" ||
        PDFJSDev.test("!PRODUCTION || TESTING")) &&
      this.appearance && !this._streams.includes(this.appearance)
    ) {
      unreachable(/* Error message here... */);
    }
```
